The pdaxrom t-iris and t-iris6 fragments hardcode LIMITS_H_TEST = true,
which makes GCC always wrap <limits.h> with an #include_next of the
target's own limits.h. When no sysroot is installed yet that include_next
finds nothing, and any configure test that includes <limits.h> fails (for
example libgcc's autoconf C-preprocessor sanity check on hosts without
/lib/cpp). The GCC default test, [ -f $(BUILD_SYSTEM_HEADER_DIR)/limits.h ],
does the right thing in both cases: self-contained while headerless,
wrapping once a sysroot with IRIX headers is present.

--- a/gcc/config/mips/t-iris
+++ b/gcc/config/mips/t-iris
@@ -11,5 +11,3 @@
 
 #undef  ENDFILE_SPEC
 #define ENDFILE_SPEC "crtend.s irix-crtn.asm"
-
-LIMITS_H_TEST = true
